WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
You know, the real gap in supply chain hiring right now?

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.500
It isn't finding planners who know their way around an Excel spreadsheet.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.500
Nope. It's actually finding the planners who can build the tool that replaces Excel.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Because for years, we've kind of been stuck in this weird split.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.500
On one side, you've got domain experts who just can't write code.

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.500
And on the other, software engineers who honestly don't even know

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.500
what a safety stock actually protects against.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.000
And what happens? They both end up shipping, well, half a solution.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.500
But, guys, that paradigm has completely shifted.

10
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.500
You literally don't need a massive data team anymore.

11
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.000
Today, just one planner, someone who really understands S&amp;OP and can wire up a simple API,

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.500
can launch a fully working forecasting engine in like a week.

13
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.500
And look, forget all the bold claims, let's look at the actual proof.

14
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.500
17. That is the exact number of live, interactive tools built by just one person

15
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.000
to solve real-world operating problems.

16
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.500
Just rapid fire here, we're talking an S&amp;OP co-pilot drafting your Monday briefs,

17
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.000
a GCC event surge forecaster, a multi echelon inventory optimizer,

18
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
oh, and an OTIF compliance platform handling over 36,000 events,

19
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.500
plus a React agent writing SQL and drafting POs.

20
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.500
And the best part, every single one of these is open and totally clickable.

21
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.500
So, what's the big through line connecting all this?

22
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.500
It's that the exact same skill used to rank trade signals across four different markets

23
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.000
is the one that ranks supply chain exceptions by revenue impact,

24
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.000
because at the end of the day, forecasting is just forecasting.

25
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.500
Which brings us to the real question.

26
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.000
What is the absolute most coveted combination

27
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
that nobody's going to be able to hire fast enough in 18 months?

28
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:49.000
It is exactly this, deep domain knowledge multiplied by actual build capability.

29
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000
And this whole new planner builder archetype,

30
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.500
it's already being prototyped right now by Vinayak Bhadani over in Dubai.

31
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.500
Look, the next generation of demand planner doesn't just sit there and use the tool,

32
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.500
they're the ones building it.

33
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.500
So, the only question left to ask yourself is, which one are you going to be?
